Hold the 787 Re-engine this round. Against hold it is worth +0.30 in S1, inside our $1B tie band, and -1.26 in S2, below our -$1B limit. Hold beats it on expectation whenever S2 carries more than about 19% weight (0.30 / 1.56). One development at a time no longer stands in the way, since the overlap is 0 years. The business case does. If you expect S1, log the $0.30B as doctrine premium. If Airbus re-engines the A350 now, H3 closes the option and hold is the better row by $1.26B. If it does not, bring the widebody case back in 2050 as a review, with:
